Commerce Hook Lab is an original workflow for producing traceable commerce
hooks, production packs, AI-video prompts, and controlled creative tests.

Design research considered the following independently licensed projects:

- motion-creative/skills (MIT): hook-writing, hook tactics, and UGC workflow
  concepts.
- Beerspitnight/cc-skills (MIT): short-form scripting and anti-generic-copy
  concepts.
- MapleShaw/seedance2.0-prompt-skill (MIT): Seedance reference and timing
  workflow concepts.
- aicontentskills/ai-video-storyboard-skill: multi-shot planning and visual
  consistency concepts. Its repository did not expose a root LICENSE during
  the July 2026 review, so no source code or text was copied.

No upstream source code or prose is included. Product truth traceability,
three-channel hook separation, deterministic validation, controlled test
design, and the manifest contract were written for this project.
